WEBVTT

00:21.440 --> 00:25.500
You've disgraced the name of Ashura Kai.

00:22.640 --> 00:25.500
Clan Leader, Ashura Kai
<i>Orcelott</i>

00:30.710 --> 00:33.160
We're sorry, Orcelott-san.

00:33.720 --> 00:37.390
We weren't expecting the 
Attack Master to join in.

00:39.260 --> 00:41.770
I mean... how could we?

00:42.250 --> 00:44.390
There's a Unique Scenario on the line.

00:44.390 --> 00:47.280
You should've expected 
top players to show up.

00:47.280 --> 00:50.750
Why didn't you do it yourself, then?

00:52.370 --> 00:54.290
I've got better things to do.

00:56.210 --> 00:57.780
Oh, yeah?

00:57.780 --> 00:59.970
[The Saint] Advanced Players Teach Beginners the Ropes  #81 [Cute]

74: Add (Advanced)
Seriously, to unlock the elite jobs you've got to at least make it to Sixburg.
How many times do I have to tell people this?
Maybe we should put it on the FAQ.

75: Alinoiyu (Beginner)
I have a question for our esteemed elders. I was picking up equipment
in Secondale when I ran into this player. He had the cutest talking bunny
with him. How can I befriend this monster?

00:58.000 --> 01:02.400
Anyway, this rabbit is definitely 
the key to some unique stuff.

01:02.710 --> 01:06.420
And we're dealing with a beginner 
who barely knows the system.

01:06.420 --> 01:08.610
Threaten him however you need to.

01:08.610 --> 01:10.280
Just get the information from him.

01:10.280 --> 01:11.170
Sir.

01:11.170 --> 01:12.380
Fine.

01:13.280 --> 01:15.630
Not that I have a problem with pet rabbits...

01:16.200 --> 01:21.390
But as Ashura Kai, shouldn't we figure 
out how to deal with <i>that</i> first?

01:28.200 --> 01:29.710
This again?

01:31.190 --> 01:33.440
I told you my policy on that.

01:33.440 --> 01:36.530
Unique monsters aren't made to be beatable.

01:36.930 --> 01:41.270
At the moment, we're the only ones who 
know that thing's spawn conditions.

01:41.270 --> 01:45.290
Just encountering it nabs us experience, 
so if we play our cards right,

01:45.530 --> 01:48.380
we can use it to increase 
Ashura Kai's battle power.

01:49.030 --> 01:51.290
There's nothing to be gained 
by fighting that thing.

01:51.290 --> 01:55.280
Going whole-hog on that fight would 
just be throwing good items away.

01:55.280 --> 01:56.260
Agreed.

02:04.110 --> 02:05.540
Ah, I figured.

02:05.540 --> 02:08.190
These people really are useless.

02:11.050 --> 02:12.760
Hey, where are you going?

02:12.760 --> 02:14.080
You're supposed to wait 
until the others arri—

02:14.080 --> 02:15.640
So sorry.

02:15.640 --> 02:17.820
I've got better things to do.

02:27.450 --> 02:28.740
Stupid woman.

02:30.130 --> 02:33.480
Ashura Kai used to get hate 
from everyone around them

02:33.480 --> 02:36.660
and made "thrive on hate" their philosophy.

02:36.660 --> 02:42.250
But since the update patch made 
player-killing a riskier venture,

02:42.250 --> 02:43.790
they've changed.

02:44.970 --> 02:46.460
Avoiding danger, seeking stability...

02:46.460 --> 02:50.440
the current Ashura Kai can't defeat <i>that</i>.

02:53.230 --> 02:54.690
Hard to believe

02:55.530 --> 02:58.680
I'm putting my neck on the 
line for one little NPC.

02:59.060 --> 03:01.200
Who would have thought?

03:02.510 --> 03:05.040
It's a huge gamble, win or lose...

03:05.740 --> 03:08.580
I'll bet everything I have, and win.

03:10.010 --> 03:11.850
To bury that Unique monster,

03:11.850 --> 03:14.340
one of the Seven Colossi...

03:15.090 --> 03:17.930
Wethermon the Tombguard.

03:22.250 --> 03:24.490
Watch me, Set-chan.

03:27.970 --> 03:32.980
<b>New Chapter
"A Bouquet Thrown With Love From the River's Edge"</b>

05:03.300 --> 05:08.470
<b>A Dazzling Sea of Trees</b>

05:06.170 --> 05:07.470
Okay, I've decided!

05:07.470 --> 05:10.450
We'll head for the 
Prismatic Forest Grotto first!

05:10.890 --> 05:13.500
Would you like to know 
my reasoning, Emul-kun?

05:13.500 --> 05:18.750
It's gonna be a pain in the ass if there're
guns and such in the ruins, so hard pass.

05:14.550 --> 05:17.930
Haven't we seen that person before?

05:18.750 --> 05:19.740
Huh? Person?

05:26.580 --> 05:31.020
I-Isn't that... That's Psyger-0, right?

05:31.460 --> 05:33.430
Talk about intimidating...

05:35.310 --> 05:38.560
Wait, is he here to get 
payback for stepping on him?!

05:42.780 --> 05:43.700
Bad news, Emul!

05:43.700 --> 05:44.550
Run!

05:44.550 --> 05:45.490
What?!

05:53.050 --> 05:55.310
Any sightings of the birdman?

05:55.810 --> 05:56.750
Nah.

05:57.080 --> 06:00.020
He might've moved on to a new area already.

06:00.750 --> 06:02.860
Clear the way!

06:02.860 --> 06:04.420
You're running so quickly!

06:04.840 --> 06:07.340
Sunraku

06:08.110 --> 06:09.450
What's with that guy?

06:09.450 --> 06:11.300
There's some weirdos out there.

06:10.340 --> 06:12.430
Sunraku

06:12.430 --> 06:14.310
Wait, look!

06:14.310 --> 06:15.520
That's Sunraku!

06:15.520 --> 06:16.270
What?!

06:17.280 --> 06:20.690
That's it! He thinks he can 
trick us with that weird armor!

06:20.690 --> 06:22.020
Thinks he's pretty clever, eh?

06:22.870 --> 06:24.040
Look at that!

06:24.040 --> 06:25.410
A monster?!

06:30.420 --> 06:32.080
And there he goes.

06:32.080 --> 06:33.660
What was that all about?

06:35.430 --> 06:36.410
There he is!

06:36.880 --> 06:38.160
Get back here, you!

06:40.170 --> 06:41.180
Damn it.

06:41.180 --> 06:43.590
Emul, let's move on to the next area!

06:43.590 --> 06:44.920
Of course!

06:47.630 --> 06:50.250
I know where he's going.

06:50.250 --> 06:53.650
He's making a beeline for the Iron Ruins.

06:53.650 --> 06:56.330
Let's tell 'em to set an ambush at the gate!

06:56.330 --> 06:58.890
Got it. We're on our way.

07:00.080 --> 07:02.180
Excuse me, Sunraku-san?!

07:02.180 --> 07:02.900
What?

07:03.110 --> 07:06.440
Wasn't our destination the 
Prismatic Forest Grotto?

07:06.440 --> 07:10.440
This is the way to the Iron 
Ruins of the Divinity!

07:10.440 --> 07:12.410
Yeah, it's a fake-out!

07:12.410 --> 07:15.910
If I went straight to my real destination, 
they'd catch on in a minute!

07:15.910 --> 07:18.150
I'll make 'em think I'm 
heading for the ruins,

07:18.150 --> 07:21.670
while I cut through an alley and head 
for the Prismatic Forest Grotto!

07:22.410 --> 07:24.670
If I can just shake 'em off for a second...

07:25.050 --> 07:27.960
They'll just go to wait for me
at the wrong gate!

07:31.630 --> 07:33.600
Damn it. Where'd he go?

07:33.600 --> 07:36.160
Just head for the gate 
that leads to the Ruins!

07:36.160 --> 07:37.180
Right.

07:45.310 --> 07:46.650
You see that, Emul?

07:46.650 --> 07:48.550
In order to truly deceive another,

07:48.550 --> 07:50.730
you must always prepare 
at least one obvious lie,

07:50.730 --> 07:54.930
one truth that seems like a lie, 
and one lie that seems truthful.

07:54.930 --> 07:56.490
How educational!

07:56.490 --> 07:59.370
I learned that from Pencilgon, actually.

08:01.440 --> 08:03.140
Okay, perfect.

08:03.140 --> 08:05.410
Deception comple—

08:11.420 --> 08:13.300
<i>How did he know?!</i>

08:17.160 --> 08:21.350
<i>Don't tell me... he's more than 
some muscle-headed gaming addict?!</i>

08:21.620 --> 08:25.480
You've received a friend request from
<b><i>Psyger-0</i></b>. Accept?

08:21.620 --> 08:25.480
No

08:21.620 --> 08:25.480
Yes

08:24.510 --> 08:25.480
Huh?

08:26.950 --> 08:28.730
A friend request?

08:30.730 --> 08:37.870
I-I'd like to... s-start as... friends.

08:38.350 --> 08:39.890
I can barely hear you, man...

08:39.890 --> 08:42.540
<i>Wait, is the player a girl?</i>

08:42.540 --> 08:48.520
<i>The friend system is proof 
of close bonds within a game.</i>

08:48.520 --> 08:53.510
<i>A friend request is an expression 
of intent to build such a bond.</i>

08:54.090 --> 08:56.360
<i>Why send me a friend request?</i>

08:56.730 --> 08:58.640
<i>Is this a plot to get my guard down?</i>

08:59.140 --> 09:02.840
<i>No... if that were the case, 
I'd be cut in half already.</i>

09:03.490 --> 09:06.300
<i>Are you trying to build 
a friendly relationship</i>

09:06.300 --> 09:10.650
<i>so I'll voluntarily spill 
info about the scenario?</i>

09:14.310 --> 09:15.930
<i>Psyger-0...</i>

09:16.520 --> 09:19.050
<i>You're observant enough to 
see through my perfect diversion</i>

09:19.050 --> 09:22.750
<i>and to suss out my true destination.</i>

09:22.750 --> 09:24.910
<i>You've got to be plotting something.</i>

09:26.490 --> 09:31.140
<i>But I'm a gamer who's been through 
all kinds of PvP before...</i>

09:31.140 --> 09:32.420
<i>So bring it on.</i>

09:36.030 --> 09:39.890
<i>I'll play into your hands
and still beat you!</i>

09:41.660 --> 09:44.390
<b><i>Sunraku </i></b>has been added to your
friend list.

09:47.870 --> 09:50.030
<i>I did it!</i>

09:56.960 --> 10:00.780
<i>When I first lost sight 
of him, I got so upset...</i>

10:01.270 --> 10:03.450
After I finally found him!

10:04.040 --> 10:09.750
The first time I came to Thirdrema, 
I traveled to the Forest Grotto first, right?

10:11.290 --> 10:13.150
<i>It was a total guess, but...</i>

10:14.480 --> 10:16.660
<i>I'm so glad I found him!</i>

10:17.850 --> 10:19.760
U-Um...

10:19.760 --> 10:26.170
I-If you'd like... I could... 
h-help you through the game...

10:26.570 --> 10:27.770
Help me?

10:28.150 --> 10:29.210
<i>I knew it!</i>

10:29.210 --> 10:33.770
<i>You're trying to get me in your debt 
and shake me down for info later!</i>

10:33.770 --> 10:39.110
Um... I'm not a huge fan of 
power-leveling my way through games.

10:39.110 --> 10:41.780
I appreciate the offer, 
but I'll have to say no.

10:44.170 --> 10:44.970
O...

10:45.790 --> 10:47.780
Of course you would!

10:47.780 --> 10:53.320
Um, so... I'm sorry if I've 
ruined any of your fun!

10:53.670 --> 10:56.210
I-I suppose I've been very rude...

10:57.210 --> 11:00.940
Then... good luck with your game!

11:00.940 --> 11:02.750
Oh... yeah.

11:02.750 --> 11:06.590
And sorry about using you 
as a stepping stool earlier.

11:06.590 --> 11:08.120
O-Oh, not at all!

11:08.120 --> 11:10.850
W-Well, another time, maybe!

11:11.150 --> 11:12.010
Right.

11:12.010 --> 11:13.800
Well... later, then.

11:19.060 --> 11:22.880
<i>Eh? She backed off pretty quickly...</i>

11:23.280 --> 11:26.500
That pioneer looked very strong indeed!

11:26.500 --> 11:28.620
Yeah, she's quite a gamer.

11:28.620 --> 11:31.640
Probably four or five times stronger than me.

11:31.640 --> 11:35.380
Though I'm sure your vorpal 
soul is by far the stronger!

11:35.380 --> 11:37.130
I appreciate that.

11:37.830 --> 11:41.530
<i>Though I wish she'd tell me what 
the hell a vorpal soul is already.</i>

11:42.950 --> 11:46.670
<i>Still... maybe I'm overthinking it?</i>

11:47.000 --> 11:50.370
<i>Well, I'll write it off as an encounter 
with a more rational Lycagon,</i>

11:50.370 --> 11:52.220
<i>put it behind me and move on!</i>

11:56.610 --> 12:01.530
That girl with him didn't 
have a name over her head.

12:01.530 --> 12:03.650
I guess she was an NPC, huh?

12:04.240 --> 12:07.670
I was so shocked, at first, 
I ended up hiding, but...

12:08.290 --> 12:12.040
One way or another, Hizutome-kun 
accepted my friend request!

12:12.260 --> 12:15.470
I've made progress, Mana-san!

12:16.430 --> 12:17.770
So tell him how you feel.

12:19.250 --> 12:20.360
Damn it.

12:20.360 --> 12:22.730
He's not heading for the ruins after all?

12:22.730 --> 12:24.010
A diversion, eh?

12:24.010 --> 12:25.990
Seems he knows what he's doing.

12:25.990 --> 12:27.690
Let's head for the Prismatic—

12:31.740 --> 12:33.940
Th-The Attack Master?!

12:33.940 --> 12:36.540
W-We'll try this one later!

13:00.360 --> 13:02.810
We can finally relax!

13:01.130 --> 13:06.970
Sheesh, even with that thing 
on, I was still recognized.

13:08.560 --> 13:11.420
Even in a cave, it's so bright!

13:11.420 --> 13:12.970
Sunraku-san!

13:13.700 --> 13:15.450
Photoluminescent moss, huh?

13:15.450 --> 13:16.810
So it's one of those deals.

13:18.730 --> 13:22.650
<i>I've been greeted by plenty of sights 
as I come out at the end of a tunnel.</i>

13:22.650 --> 13:27.240
<i>Rifles pointed at me, shooting stars 
passing in front of my eyes...</i>

13:28.140 --> 13:31.470
<i>But this is really what 
it says on the tin, huh?</i>

13:28.340 --> 13:33.250
<b>Prismatic Forest Grotto</b>

14:01.750 --> 14:04.530
<b>Storage Papillon</b>

14:07.760 --> 14:10.530
<b>Empire Worker Bee</b>

14:16.890 --> 14:19.670
<b>Mimic Mantis</b>

14:22.900 --> 14:25.170
<b>Quad Beetle</b>

14:29.350 --> 14:30.670
Awesome!

14:30.670 --> 14:33.430
Nothing beats the excitement of a new area!

14:37.770 --> 14:41.610
Your little tummy sways 
in such an alluring way...

14:41.610 --> 14:44.250
I'm counting on a pricey item drop from you.

14:41.980 --> 14:44.230
<b>Marsh Daggers
</b>equipped

14:44.250 --> 14:47.940
I'm a little low on cash 
from stocking up on items.

14:48.950 --> 14:51.450
Sunraku-san, fight!

14:54.150 --> 14:55.490
Gotcha!

14:59.420 --> 15:02.990
Pretty light on your wings 
despite that big ol' potbelly.

15:02.990 --> 15:06.380
But a butterfly's speed

15:06.790 --> 15:08.130
is still too slow!

15:11.130 --> 15:12.800
Aha!

15:13.040 --> 15:14.620
I thought so!

15:14.620 --> 15:18.810
If I don't damage the stomach, 
I can snag it as an item!

15:19.080 --> 15:23.310
<b>Storage Papillon Nectar Pouch 
Used by the Storage Papillon to store its nectar. It's very fragile, so it's difficult to obtain with the nectar intact. The nectar is fun to eat and fun to throw.</b>

15:19.820 --> 15:23.310
What's this say?
"Storage Papillon Nectar Pouch"?

15:23.800 --> 15:25.400
"Fun to throw"?

15:25.400 --> 15:28.120
That was quite a skillful 
display, Sunraku-san!

15:28.120 --> 15:29.220
You said it!

15:29.220 --> 15:32.250
Let's keep gathering up those item drops!

15:32.250 --> 15:33.970
And earn much money!

15:33.970 --> 15:36.550
Then beat the area boss!

15:36.550 --> 15:38.850
We fear nothing!

15:49.340 --> 15:50.660
There it is.

15:51.860 --> 15:54.240
I fear I don't see it.

15:54.220 --> 15:55.850
<b>Throwing Knife 
</b>equipped.

15:54.240 --> 15:55.850
Well, just you watch.

15:55.850 --> 15:58.470
You bought a knife?

15:58.470 --> 16:00.070
A Throwing Knife.

16:00.070 --> 16:02.730
Since melee is my only combat option,

16:02.730 --> 16:06.730
Practical Training  Opponent 5
Toxic Eagle

16:02.730 --> 16:06.730
I got pretty traumatized by 
the shitbird in the arena.

16:07.260 --> 16:11.440
It's a consumable item, but it's an 
invaluable way to attack from a distance.

16:17.320 --> 16:20.040
I knew you were there, you mantis bastard!

16:20.620 --> 16:23.290
You keep running off and 
camouflaging yourself...

16:23.710 --> 16:27.420
Just turn into loot already!

16:25.940 --> 16:27.960
Spiral Edge

16:33.370 --> 16:34.970
How truly brilliant!

16:35.190 --> 16:39.950
Okay, so those guys are a cinch 
without their camouflaged ambushes.

16:39.950 --> 16:42.730
And you've collected no shortage of items!

16:42.910 --> 16:47.980
<b>Storage Papillon Nectar Pouch
 Empire Worker Bee Pollen Hair
 Empire Hunter Bee Stinger
 Empire Hunter Bee Mandible
 Mimic Mantis Stealth Wing
 Mimic Mantis Scythe Arm</b>

16:43.660 --> 16:46.400
Yeah, it's going pretty smooth,

16:46.400 --> 16:47.980
but there's one I haven't beaten yet...

16:52.820 --> 16:54.490
Speak of the devil!

17:05.270 --> 17:06.530
He's a hefty guy!

17:06.530 --> 17:11.130
Beetle boy there's gotta be 
at least five meters long.

17:11.130 --> 17:13.010
That's a Quad Beetle!

17:13.740 --> 17:15.510
<b>Empire Hunter Bee</b>

17:14.050 --> 17:15.510
Is it fighting?

17:15.510 --> 17:19.430
It's drinking tree sap 
on the Empire Bees' turf!

17:19.430 --> 17:21.510
Yeah, that's a way to piss 'em off.

17:22.240 --> 17:24.520
<b>Empire Queen Bee</b>

17:37.520 --> 17:38.640
Look at that!

17:38.640 --> 17:42.490
The Empire Bees are attacking 
en masse on their queen's orders.

17:42.490 --> 17:45.370
But Quad Beetle is unaffected 
by their stings!

17:45.370 --> 17:48.540
Upon whom shall the goddess 
of victory smile?!

17:48.540 --> 17:51.210
Emul-san on color commentary, 
what do you think?

17:51.210 --> 17:52.700
C-Color commentary?!

17:52.700 --> 17:55.610
I-I don't know <i>that</i> much about them!

17:55.610 --> 17:59.820
At least say "There's no telling 
how it'll turn out just yet!"

17:59.820 --> 18:02.150
Just improvise, girl. It's all about feeling.

18:02.150 --> 18:04.180
This is all very tricky.

18:04.400 --> 18:07.810
The fierce battle between 
monsters is escalating!

18:07.810 --> 18:10.180
Quad Beetle is attacking 
with all four of his horns

18:10.180 --> 18:12.440
as he proceeds, undaunted, to the nest!

18:12.920 --> 18:15.480
Is this the end of the Empire Bees?!

18:15.480 --> 18:16.470
Well, Emul-san?

18:16.470 --> 18:18.460
Give the people a word!

18:18.460 --> 18:21.070
I-It's a very large bug!

18:22.110 --> 18:23.330
What in the world?

18:25.490 --> 18:26.590
Goodness me!

18:26.590 --> 18:28.220
The unrelenting wave of attacks

18:28.220 --> 18:32.210
has created an exploitable crack 
in the Quad Beetle's armor!

18:32.210 --> 18:36.050
The Empire Bee Queen gives 
the crucial order to attack!

18:36.050 --> 18:39.880
Quad Beetle's in big trouble now!

18:48.420 --> 18:50.050
And it's done!

18:50.050 --> 18:55.190
Once he had her in firing range, 
Quad Beetle flew right into the queen!

18:55.420 --> 18:58.840
With their queen gone, 
the bees are scattering!

19:02.710 --> 19:05.450
And right back to his meal, huh?

19:05.790 --> 19:08.460
With a near-death injury and everything.

19:08.830 --> 19:10.580
That's what I call a kingly air.

19:20.760 --> 19:22.730
He's coming right for us!

19:22.730 --> 19:25.240
Oh, gracious!

19:25.240 --> 19:29.620
Hey, I wanted to collect 
those Empire Bee drop items!

19:29.620 --> 19:31.770
What's with the hair-trigger temper?

19:31.770 --> 19:33.980
I didn't do anything to him!

19:33.980 --> 19:38.250
Perhaps he thinks you were there for the sap!

19:38.610 --> 19:40.280
Sap, huh?

19:41.420 --> 19:42.800
Storage Papillon Nectar Pouch

19:43.030 --> 19:44.570
Let's try it!

19:55.930 --> 19:58.460
Looks like he really was after the nectar.

20:00.470 --> 20:04.910
Those cracks in your armor 
the Empire Bees left...

20:04.910 --> 20:07.430
I can't leave them unexploited!

20:29.530 --> 20:30.610
Hell yeah!

20:30.610 --> 20:32.370
Make them do the work and 
reap all the profits!

20:32.370 --> 20:39.130
Dropped Items
 Quad Beetle Horn
 Quad Beetle Mandible
 Quad Beetle Shell
 Quad Beetle Elytron

20:33.200 --> 20:35.980
I've got an inventory full of items now,

20:35.980 --> 20:38.730
so I'll hold off on any 
more collecting for now.

20:40.540 --> 20:44.280
Exploiting the labor of others 
doesn't quite seem fair to me.

20:44.280 --> 20:45.930
What're you talking about?

20:45.930 --> 20:47.920
It's a bug-eat-bug world.

20:47.920 --> 20:50.140
You gotta do what it takes 
to be the last one standing.

20:50.140 --> 20:52.480
Harrumph.

20:54.690 --> 20:58.600
The area boss here is a spider, right?

20:58.990 --> 21:00.100
Yes, indeed!

21:00.100 --> 21:01.730
It's called the Clown Spider!

21:01.730 --> 21:04.970
So... we're probably getting close.

21:11.920 --> 21:12.980
Okay!

22:53.930 --> 23:01.190
<b>SLF Mini</b>

22:54.640 --> 22:58.420
<i><i>SLF</i></i> Theater!

22:57.740 --> 23:01.180
<i><b>What Kind of Person Is Kuon Amane?</b></i>

22:58.420 --> 22:59.950
Mini!

23:01.190 --> 23:13.070
<b>Kuon Amane 
The Celebrity Model
on Fashion's Bleeding Edge</b>

